cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Harmonized U.S. Fetal Death Microdata, 1982-2022"
message: "If you use this dataset, please cite it using the metadata in this file."
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: Plutchok
    given-names: Yoel
    email: yoelyehudaplutchok@gmail.com
abstract: >-
  A modern, researcher-ready release of harmonized U.S. fetal death microdata
  for cross-year stillbirth research. Spans 41 years (1982-2022) of NCHS
  public-use fetal death files reconciled into a single Parquet file with one
  stable schema. Three revisions of the Standard Report of Fetal Death (1978,
  1989, 2003) and staggered state adoption are bridged via documented
  crosswalks. 2,352,011 total records (~1.99 million NVSR-comparable). Validation:
  88 byte-exact checks against published NCHS/NVSR statistics (55 V1 + 23 V2/V3
  counts + 10 V2/V2.1 rates); all 41 per-year counts and all 10 per-year rates
  match exactly. Companion to the U.S. Natality Harmonization Project (Zenodo
  concept DOI 10.5281/zenodo.19363074), which supplies the live-birth
  denominators needed for fetal mortality rate computation.
keywords:
  - stillbirth
  - fetal death
  - perinatal epidemiology
  - National Vital Statistics System
  - NCHS
  - data harmonization
  - cross-revision
  - 1978 revision
  - 1989 revision
  - 2003 revision
  - public health
  - epidemiology
  - United States
